                <pb facs="0326" n="220" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg220"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1906-08-30">August 30,
                        1906</date></hi>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Referring to Mr. Rockhill’s telegram of August 30, Mr. Adee instructs him to
                    make demand in accord with British, which is understood to be that, until
                    customs are established throughout Manchuria, no duties be levied at
                    Newchwang.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
